const List<dynamic> faqData = [{'title': 'Getting Started', 'icon': 'rocket-outline', 'color': '#EE9A4C', 'items': [{'q': 'What is HindiMitra?', 'a': 'HindiMitra is an interactive app for learning Hindi reading and writing. You practice the Devanagari script through guided tracing, quizzes, flashcards, story reading, and more. The app tracks your progress with stars, points, streaks, and badges.'}, {'q': 'How do I create an account?', 'a': 'You can sign up with your email and password from the login screen, or tap "Continue as Guest" to start without an account. Guest progress is saved on your device only. With an account, your progress syncs to the cloud so you can access it from any device.'}, {'q': 'What age groups is this for?', 'a': 'HindiMitra is designed for three age groups: Kids 3-6 (simple, visual learning), Kids 7-10 (more detailed exercises), and Adults (comprehensive practice). You select your age group during onboarding, and the app adapts accordingly.'}, {'q': 'Is HindiMitra free?', 'a': 'Yes! Basic features including letter writing practice, flashcards, letter quizzes, word reading, and most reading activities are free. Premium features like the AI Pronunciation Coach, Story Reading with comprehension, and Parent Dashboard require an upgrade.'}]}, {'title': 'Writing Module', 'icon': 'pencil-outline', 'color': '#6E4EDF', 'items': [{'q': 'How does letter writing practice work?', 'a': 'Each letter has 4 progressive stages. You draw on a canvas using your finger (mobile) or mouse (web). The app evaluates your strokes and awards 1-3 stars based on accuracy. Complete 3 successful attempts to advance to the next stage.'}, {'q': 'What are the 4 writing stages?', 'a': 'Stage 1 (Guided Tracing): Trace over a visible ghost letter. Stage 2 (Faded Ghost): The letter is barely visible for gentle guidance. Stage 3 (Freehand + Reference): Write freely with a small reference in the corner. Stage 4 (From Memory): Write after hearing the pronunciation — no visual help!'}, {'q': 'How do I practice Matra (vowel marks)?', 'a': 'Go to the Write tab and select "Matra Practice" from the letter grid. You\'ll learn how vowel marks (matras) attach to consonants to form syllables. There\'s also a Matra Quiz to test your knowledge of combining letters with vowel marks.'}, {'q': 'What is Word Writing?', 'a': 'Word Writing lets you practice writing complete Hindi words letter by letter. The app shows the target word and highlights which letter to write next. Available from the Write tab — great for building fluency after mastering individual letters.'}]}, {'title': 'Reading Module', 'icon': 'book-outline', 'color': '#4EC58A', 'items': [{'q': 'What reading activities are available?', 'a': 'There are 11 reading activities: Flashcards (swipe & learn), Letter Quiz (pick correct pronunciation), Word Reading (syllable-by-syllable), Sentence Building (arrange words), Story Reading (premium), Pronunciation Coach (premium), Picture Match (visual vocabulary), Word Builder (unscramble letters), Fill in the Blank (grammar), Hindi Numbers (0-20), and Letter Sound Quiz (audio recognition).'}, {'q': 'How do Flashcards work?', 'a': 'Swipe through letter cards to browse the Hindi alphabet. Tap any card to flip it and see the pronunciation, romanized spelling, an example word, and its meaning. You can also tap the speaker icon to hear the correct pronunciation.'}, {'q': 'What is the Letter Sound Quiz?', 'a': 'You see a Hindi letter and hear three pronunciation options. Pick the correct sound! It tests your listening comprehension and letter-sound association. Get 7 or more correct out of 10 to earn stars and see a celebration.'}, {'q': 'How does Story Reading work?', 'a': 'Read simple Hindi stories with word-by-word audio support — tap any word to hear it. After reading, answer 3 comprehension questions to test understanding. Stories include speed controls (0.5x, 1x, 1.5x) for audio playback. This is a Premium feature.'}, {'q': 'What is the Pronunciation Coach?', 'a': 'The AI Pronunciation Coach lets you listen to correct Hindi pronunciation, then practice speaking it yourself. It provides feedback to help you improve. This is a Premium feature available from the Read tab.'}]}, {'title': 'Progress & Rewards', 'icon': 'trophy-outline', 'color': '#F2CE58', 'items': [{'q': 'How do stars and points work?', 'a': 'You earn 1-3 stars per writing attempt based on accuracy. Points are calculated as: stars x 10 x current stage number. So a 3-star result on Stage 3 earns 90 points! Stars and points accumulate across all activities and contribute to your level.'}, {'q': 'What are badges?', 'a': 'There are 14 achievement badges you can earn: First Letter, Vowel Master, 7-Day Streak, 100 Stars, Speed Writer, Perfect Score, Consonant Pro, Monthly Streak, 500 Stars, Reading Star, Night Owl, Early Bird, Word Wizard, and Point Master. Tap earned badges on the Rewards tab to see a celebration!'}, {'q': 'How does the daily goal work?', 'a': 'Set how many letters you want to practice each day (default is 3). The circular ring on your Home screen fills up as you practice. Completing your daily goal counts toward your streak. Keep your streak alive by practicing every day!'}]}, {'title': 'Account & Settings', 'icon': 'settings-outline', 'color': '#5C6BC0', 'items': [{'q': 'How do I change my name?', 'a': 'Go to the Profile tab and tap "Edit Profile." You can update your display name in the popup that appears. Your name shows on the Home screen greeting and Leaderboard.'}, {'q': 'Can I delete my account?', 'a': 'Yes. Go to Profile → Settings → scroll down to "Delete Account." This permanently removes all your data from the cloud, including progress, stats, and letter history. This action cannot be undone.'}, {'q': 'Do notifications work on web?', 'a': 'Push notifications (daily reminders and streak alerts) are available on mobile devices only. When using the web version, notification toggles in Settings are disabled with an info message explaining this.'}]}];

